; A count of a match is the size of the bag match gives, for numbers of
; every representation: integers, floats, rationals and big integers meet
; by value, exactly (2^53 + 1 is not the float 2^53).  Each count is
; printed beside its collection, sorted; the queries run twice, so the
; first ones read cold scans and the rest the indexes a warm space keeps.
(k a 0) (j 0)
(k a 1) (j 1)
(k a -1) (j -1)
(k a 2) (j 2)
(k a 0.5) (j 0.5)
